From cf609d24cf62bdd1d49f432730c716f7d99b5e36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:04:16 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] kcm_lookandfeel: theme list read in batches after the
 first frame, Apply dialog built on first use, Day/Night as a Form
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Gallery (main) + Form (Day/Night) + gallery sub-page (Light/Dark choice), docs/page-design.md. Config keys,
KLookAndFeelManager calls, the apply flags and plasmashell D-Bus call are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy
work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- Day/Night page is now a Form: "Global themes:" (Light and Dark previews, each opens the chooser sub-page), a
  "Switching" section with "Wait until the computer is idle before switching" (checkbox, no trailing colon, help in a
  ContextualHelpButton) and an indented "Idle time before switching:" spin box (disabled, not hidden, while the checkbox
  is off), and "Configure Day/Night Cycle…" as the link out at the end (was first). The intro sentence is wrapped at
  gridUnit*20. (HIG-001/005/006, HIG-057: nouns for sections.)
- Apply dialog: "The following will be applied by this Global Theme:" -> "This Global Theme will apply:". The detailed list
  is one Kirigami.FormLayout with noun sections "Layout" and "Appearance" (was two twin FormLayouts with
  "Layout settings:" / "Appearance settings:" labels). "Desktop layout" is now disabled, not hidden, while Plasma is
  locked (before it read the checkbox's own always-true `enabled`, so the lock was never applied there).
- Empty state: Kirigami.PlaceholderMessage "No Global Themes found" (was an empty grid); busy indicator only after 150 ms.
- Thumbnails (page and chooser) load with Image.asynchronous.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_lookandfeel.tsv (outer repo); old wording added to the page aliases in
  ia/layout.json. All 31 inventory rows kept, `inventory_check.py --kcm kcm_lookandfeel --strict`: 0 lost.
- Not changed: the toolbar switch "Switch to Dark Mode at Night" still swaps the gallery for the Day/Night page (apply()
  skips the theme apply while it is on), Save Current Theme sub-page, Get New.

Speed (cause found in code, kcms/lookandfeel/kcm.cpp):
- The KCMLookandFeel constructor called loadModel() synchronously: listPackages("Plasma/LookAndFeel"), then
  loadPackage() for every package a second time, filePath("defaults"/"layouts") on each, then
  KLookAndFeelManager::packageContents() (reads the package's defaults/layouts config) for each row, all before the page
  QML was created. Preview PNGs were decoded synchronously per card (Image without asynchronous), and the "Apply <name>?"
  Kirigami.Dialog with its StackView and option pages was created with the page.
- Now: the constructor only sets up the model; loadModel() runs from QTimer::singleShot(0) and fills the model in ~8 ms
  batches (loadNextBatch), same order (sorted by name) and same filter; new property modelLoading drives the busy/empty
  state; the selected theme's contents are refreshed on rowsInserted. The dialog sits in a Loader (active on first
  click). Thumbnails are asynchronous.
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: kcm.selectedContents = undefined (RESET) replaces the old `kcm.selectedItems = undefined`
(a property that does not exist); the dialog is created inside Loader{Component{}} and still resolves `root`/ids by
scope as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
